# Task 2: Process Identity (PID and PPID)

## Objective

To identify the Process ID (PID) and Parent Process ID (PPID) of a running program using C.

## 1. C Source Code


#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>

int main() {
    // Get current Process ID
    pid_t my_pid = getpid();

    // Get Parent Process ID
    pid_t my_ppid = getppid();

    printf("My PID is: %d\n", my_pid);
    printf("My Parent PID is: %d\n", my_ppid);

    printf("Sleeping for 20 seconds...\n");
    sleep(20);

    return 0;
}
```

## 2. Compilation and Execution

**Compile the program:**

```bash
gcc task2.c -o task2
```

**Run the program in the background:**

```bash
./task2 &
```

## 3. Process Verification

Check the running process:

```bash
pgrep -a task2
```

Verify the PID and PPID using:

```bash
ps -p <PID> -o pid,ppid,cmd
```

Replace `<PID>` with the actual PID displayed by your program.

## 4. Expected Output

```text
My PID is: 1980
My Parent PID is: 1
Sleeping for 20 seconds...
```

Example process verification:

```text
PID     PPID    CMD
1980     1    ./task2
```

*Note: PID and PPID values will vary depending on the system.*

